      "post_id": "891373473443",
      "post_type": "announcement",
      "title": "Portion for the end-sem exam - Everything discussed in the class after the mid-sem exam ti",
      "text": "Portion for the end-sem exam - Everything discussed in the class after the mid-sem exam till the class on Monday 16th Nov, (excluding Peano's axioms) . \n\nTopics include :  1. Functions - injection, surjection, bijections, composition, inverse ( examples, theorems)  2. Cardinality - Finite, countable, uncountable sets, Cantor's diagonal argument( examples - \\Q is countable, (0,1) is uncountable, \\R is uncountable, other theorems ) 3. Induction , Strong induction, Well ordering principle  their applications, Equivalence of these statements. (examples, theorems)  4. Proof of - 3 blackbox statements used in the lectures on countability and uncountability 5. Construction of \\Z from natural numbers , Properties-  (e.g. associativity - addition and multiplication) 6. Group theory - Defn of a group, abelian group, cyclic group, subgroup,  examples, theorems - Every subgroup of \\Z is of the form nZ for some n in \\N. Every subgroup of a cyclic group is cyclic ( an application of induction and WOP)\n\nAll the best for exams.",
